ll,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"C3b (d074) plan PASS+signed — validated bounded template. Empirical drained-scan census (definitive): ALL rows in every remaining slice need active treatment (cut-to-seam or read-via marker); ZERO pure removals (credential-boundary files' JIRA_* reads are still composition-owner, not auto-owned). Exact row counts: C3a reconciler=57 (across ~35 files — WARRANTS decomposition), C3c cli=26, C3d llm=23. Default=cut; owned-in-place only for bounded test-only/kill-switch/subprocess-env-control allowlist. Coupling lesson: live-resolved reads (e.g. push mode) cut to a live-per-call resolver, not compose-once.","timestamp":1787106735919180001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLOSE: close gate(s) bypassed by user approval — no completion/signature attestation was signed. Reason: \"Umbrella task S7.3: all 7 child slices closed with their own completion-verifier + CI Verified+1; LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS EMPTY on main (config-ownership gate exit 0). The [operator-attested] provider/AWS-canary AC belongs to the landed S1-S6 child slices which attested it at their own close; this umbrella produced no new canary evidence.\". Session: 74517a190e.","timestamp":1787149710484509001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR-ATTESTED CANARY EVIDENCE (S7.3 — cut legacy ambient reads / drain exceptions / remove facades) — session d83fb4f6fd, run 2026-08-19 (America/Los_Angeles).\n\nSame canary set and disposition as the S7 parent (aabf); recorded here for this umbrella's operator-attested AC.\n\n1) Bounded-live provider (live-call): bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8 (AWS Bedrock; one-run/one-Agent budget), review-plan PASS on 3199/aabf/e215/075b this session, retry count 0, no cross-provider/anonymous fallback, no leakage.\n2) AWS review-bot (live-call, hosted): LLM-Review +1 on Gerrit changes 1905, 1902, 1901; auth via op-cert startup path; retry 0.\n3) op-cert (SIMULATION / narrower — DISCLOSED GAP): exclusive-startup-source, 0700/0600 process-owned copy, context-local signer, restart-only replacement, no-runtime-SSM/boto invariants exercised THIS SESSION by offline oracles only (91 passed), not a live SSM/boto fetch; the live op-cert path is separately evidenced by the hosted review-bot boot (canary 2). Hence privilege_posture=narrower.\n4) Reconciler check (live-call): bridge check-access vs live Jira REB — create/label/property-write/JQL-search/property-read/delete all PROBE_PASS (second run; first run one JQL index-lag miss, no auth failure); token never logged; fail-closed-on-missing-project confirmed.\n5) Reconciler dry-run/live (hosted): bridge status FOREIGN pass=2026-08-19T16:34:03 environment=reconciler; bridge fsck clean over the REB binding set; retry 0.\n\nLEGACY_EXCEPTIONS empty on main (config-ownership gate exit 0); all 7 child slices closed with their own completion-verifier + CI Verified+1. Offline correctness backstop: 295 GREEN (91 auth/security + 204 RP-04/provider). No credential value/path recorded. Rollback: none required; retain the S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor.","timestamp":1787168827736247001}],"created_at":1787081610794907001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b46ff4c2-5239-479e-b963-c172ca9f9121","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8"},{"link_uuid":"db920031-914c-4544-8e0c-8960fb6054a4","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"735b-cec9-fd08-4851"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n~110 direct ambient `os.getenv`/`os.environ`/`load_config` reads (plus backend property reloads and configurable adapter defaults) currently sit BELOW the approved composition seams across the reconciler engine, store, snapshot, io, cli, commands, llm/workflow, and the MCP server. RP-04 is not complete while these legacy ambient reads can return values inconsistently under an in-progress operation or bypass the central seam. The ownership gate's initial legacy-exception set (slice C1) must reach EMPTY. This slice also carries the MCP `mcp_server` `load_config()`-per-call cutover deferred from RP-04 S5.\n\n## Outcome\nEvery below-seam ambient config/credential read, backend reload, and configurable adapter default is either cut to compose through the approved seam (operation snapshot / startup binding / provider boundary) or, for genuine test-only controls and protocol constants, registered with an exact `path+symbol+rationale` entry. The ownership gate then passes on the real tree with an EMPTY legacy-exception set. Legacy facades, migration switches, per-job ambient reloads, and migration exceptions are removed only after their focused suites pass. All S1-S6 behavioral suites remain green and provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged (approved deltas recorded).\n\n## Plan\n1. Iterate subsystem-by-subsystem (reconciler engine; store/snapshot/io; cli/commands; llm/workflow; mcp_server/_mcp_auth). For each below-seam read: cut-to-seam OR register with rationale.\n2. Drain the legacy-exception set to empty; remove legacy facades/switches only after each subsystem's suite passes.\n3. Record redacted snapshot-fingerprint / provider-neutral outcome comparisons and any approved behavior delta.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- The ownership gate (C1) passes on the REAL tree with an EMPTY legacy-exception set and no path-glob exceptions.\n- All S1-S6 behavioral suites pass after each subsystem cutover and after legacy-facade removal (they are the correctness oracle; the AST gate supplements them).\n- Redacted operation snapshot fingerprints and provider-neutral outcomes before/after are equal except for explicitly recorded, justified deltas.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nDo not remove a legacy facade until its focused suite and bounded path pass; before removal, rollback selects the facade. At contract phase, retain only the S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor; rollback below it is unsupported and documented. Stored ticket/event/bridge/binding formats are unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The real tree has no direct ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable adapter default below approved seams; every declared config/credential name has one owner; the legacy exception set is EMPTY; no exception uses a path glob.\n- [x] All S1-S6 behavioral suites pass after legacy removal; redacted fingerprints/provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged except for recorded approved deltas.\n- [x] Legacy facades, switches, per-job ambient reloads, and migration exceptions are removed only after their proof passes; documented rollback retains the S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Bounded provider, AWS review-bot/op-cert, and reconciler check/dry-run/live canaries pass with required redacted evidence (run/change ids, timestamps, selected provider/auth-source kind, retry/cache counters, redacted fingerprint/outcome, rollback decision) and no unauthorized fallback or leakage.\n  provenance: environment=hosted-production-and-local-bounded; principal=aws-review-bot-reconciler-and-bounded-provider; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — bounded-live provider bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8 ran review-plan this session with retry count 0; AWS review-bot cast LLM-Review +1 on Gerrit changes 1905, 1902, 1901; live reconciler check-access against Jira project REB passed every probe step; a hosted reconciler foreign pass was witnessed at 2026-08-19T16:34:03; the op-cert startup-source and SSM path were exercised this session only by offline behavioral oracles with no production SSM or boto privilege, hence the narrower posture; no unauthorized fallback and no credential value or path recorded; rollback decision is to retain the snapshot-envelope compatibility floor.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config/credential reads to seams incl MCP load_config cutover; remove legacy facades."},{"path":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py","reason":"Drain the legacy-exception set to empty."},{"path":"tests/external/","reason":"Canary/bounded-live evidence harness."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","force_close_reason":"Umbrella task S7.3: all 7 child slices closed with their own completion-verifier + CI Verified+1; LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS EMPTY on main (config-ownership gate exit 0). The [operator-attested] provider/AWS-canary AC belongs to the landed S1-S6 child slices which attested it at their own close; this umbrella produced no new canary evidence.","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1787168755247863001,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8"],["depends_on","735b-cec9-fd08-4851"],["parent","aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4","parent_status_uuid":"125d5315-28f9-4677-bd76-f49bb2e37376","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"075b-1479-dcb7-40ab","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.3 — Cut legacy ambient reads to seams, drain exceptions to empty, remove facades","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["45dc9c2c-ca43-4382-afdf-90bb89ad75bc","8bfeea2c-589d-4a37-9569-a207f46a7c05","fbc1a785-cf41-44d4-b239-24e5296e7f2b","4d1379c2-a011-4c3f-8b31-5f91ef3ee7e2","acaec3b8-9f64-40a6-b693-a962585a380c","83980ce4-8bd5-4a1b-870a-d68ab9e094fb","ceadbd1c-94c3-4980-923f-9134fe719c05","019fbd82-e932-4fbe-b653-850a44197f41","125d5315-28f9-4677-bd76-f49bb2e37376","113ea590-be0f-46fd-9c45-7b8d2ce76cc3","dabfa376-129d-4fe6-a45d-ed8f2fa4a968","d09127d4-e066-4fa0-a432-4b959d38cbf7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3